WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:03.600
Another Thing That Doctor Bright Is&nbsp;
Not Allowed To Do At The Foundation:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:06.960
No ending reports with lyrics from&nbsp;
"The Fresh Prince of Bel-Air".&nbsp;

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:11.600
Sometimes work at the SCP Foundation can get a&nbsp;
bit grueling, so Dr. Bright tries to “brighten”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:15.600
everyone’s day with a little pop culture&nbsp;
reference or two. However, after a report&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:20.880
on SCP-096’s potential origins concluded with&nbsp;
“In West of the Arctic, born and raised, in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:25.360
mountains is where he spent most of his days.”&nbsp;
His colleagues agreed that enough was enough.&nbsp;

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:29.600
However, after he submitted a formal&nbsp;
request, he was given certain allowances.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:34.000
Mainly, he can use lyrics from Safety Dance,&nbsp;
as the majority of the research staff still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:39.760
find them funny. Most notably, he ended a report&nbsp;
on SCP-049 with: “You can cure if you want to,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:43.440
you can leave your friends behind. Cause&nbsp;
your friends got plague and if they’ve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:48.080
got plague then they’re no friends of mine!”
After his accompanying dance nearly broke a window&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:53.680
and triggered a containment breach of SCP-173,&nbsp;
however, his boogying privileges were revoked.

